OL,3,GNEWSARoyal Marines and soldiers settle
OL,4,AMoD asbestos claim
OL,5,
OL,6,FA group of 256 Royal Marines and
OL,7,Fsoldiers, who claimed the Ministry of
OL,8,FDefence (MoD) had "knowingly" exposed
OL,9,Fthem to asbestos, have settled out of
OL,10,Fcourt for an undisclosed sum.
OL,12,FCourt proceedings were issued against
OL,13,Fthe MOD in February 2024 by the group,
OL,14,Ffrom Plymouth and Scotland, claiming
OL,15,Ftheir employer had breached the Human
OL,16,FRights Act.
OL,18,FThe potential exposure was said to have
OL,19,Ftaken place in Latvia in 2018 and 2019
OL,20,Fover two exercises, with a sample
OL,21,Fcollected by a marine at the time found
OL,22,Fto contain asbestos.
OL,23,APub: 20-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,347,340,200,160,0,100
